fied on this form, that the information specified on this form\nL143@P1: is true and correct, and that I am the head of the agency taking this action,\nL144@P1: or a designee of the head of the agency, and am authorized to make this certification.\nL145@P1: SIGNATURE GF AGENCY HEAD OR DESIGNEE DATE\nL146@P1: 5/20/2026\nL147@P1: SIGNATORY\nL148@P1: cutive Officer, Structural Pest Control Board\nL149@P1: For use by Office of Administrative Law (OAL) only\nL150@P1: ENDORSED APPROVED\nL151@P1: )\nL152@P1-2: Office ot Administrative Law postponement of not more than six (6) months will not be required to file a new\nL153@P2: application for examination prescribed in section 1940.1.\nL154@P2: NOTE: Authority cited: Section 8525, Business and Professions Code. Reference:\nL155@P2: Sections 8560 and 8674, Business and Professions Code.\nL156@P2: 1942. Applicant Failing Operator's or Field Representative's Application for Re\u0002Examination.\nL157@P2: (a) An applicant who does not pass anfails the operator's or field representative's\nL158@P2: examination specified in section 1940 may request to take another examination\nL159@P2: within six (6) months thereafterby submitting on the samean application by paying an\nL160@P2: additional examination fee for re-examination to the board, accompanied by such\nL161@P2: statements and documents as required by this subsection, in hard copy to the\nL162@P2: board's current physical address listed on its website or electronically through the\nL163@P2: board's online portal accessible through the board's website. A completed\nL164@P2: application for re-examination shall include the application fee required by section\nL165@P2: 1948 and the following information:\nL166@P2: ill Applicant's full legal name (Last Name, First Name, and Middle Name).\nL167@P2: (2) Applicant's Examination ID Number.\nL168@P2: (3) Applicant's current mailing address.\nL169@P2: (4) Applicant's telephone number.\nL170@P2: (5) Applicant's email address.\nL171@P2: (6) A statement signed by the applicant under penalty of perjury that the information\nL172@P2: provided in the application for examination is true and correct.\nL173@P2: (b) Once the board approves an applicant for re-examination, the board shall send a\nL174@P2: written approval notice to the examination vendor, PSI Services LLC (PSI), and to\nL175@P2: the applicant by email or, if an email address is not provided by the applicant, by\nL176@P2: United States Postal Service to the mailing address the applicant provided in their\nL177@P2: application for re-examination.\nL178@P2: ill The approval notice shall contain the web-site address, email address, telephone\nL179@P2: number, and mailing address of PSI, specify that the applicant is responsible for\nL180@P2: complying with the requirements in paragraphs (2) and (3) of this subsection, and\nL181@P2: specify that failure to appear for the examination is grounds for forfeiture of the\nL182@P2: examination fee, unless the applicant requests and is granted a postponement in\nL183@P2: accordance with section 1941.\nL184@P2: (2) The applicant shall contact PSI to schedule an examination date, time, and site\nL185@P2: location .\nL186@P2: (3) The applicant shall appear at the designated PSI examination site location at\nL187@P2: their scheduled date and time, and the applicant shall present their acceptable\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNotice of Approved Regulatory Action CCR 111 Review of Applications (https://www.cab.ca.gov/docs/regulation_changes/2025-26/ccr_111_noara.pdf)\nciteturn1203view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 4; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1185view0\",\"id\":34}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDPR 25-004 Text of Final Regulations (https://www.cdpr.ca.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/dpr25-004_oal_final_text_ppe_use.pdf)\ncit